{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>There shall be seven years of famine. It is the thing that I have spoken, etc.</b> There is a question here: why did Joseph begin the interpretation with the seven years of famine? He should have begun with the interpretation of the seven years of plenty that precede the years of famine. And further, it is difficult what he said, 'It is the thing that I have spoken' — as though he were proving his words in order to establish his interpretation; and what proof is there here? And I say that this is its meaning: that Joseph reasoned with his intellect that there would be years of plenty and years of famine, because he saw the matter of eating in the cows and swallowing in the ears of grain — that the lean ate and swallowed the fat. And the main proof was specifically from the ears of grain, for from the eating of the cows he could prove nothing — that he was speaking of years of plenty and famine — for perhaps the dream would be fulfilled literally, that seven lean cows would eat seven fat cows, or perhaps its interpretation is that seven wicked men, poor and empty, would eat seven righteous and good men — either their wealth or their bodies — for this is found in reality, that the wicked lays siege to the righteous, as it says (Habakkuk 1:13), ״בְּבַלַּע רָשָׁע צַדִּיק מִמֶּנּוּ״." "However, once he told him the matter of the swallowing of the ears of grain — behold, this swallowing is impossible to fulfill literally, for the ears of grain, being things of vegetable growth, have no living spirit by which one could swallow the other. And even if we say that it is a metaphor and simile, none the less, a person is not shown something that is entirely impossible, just as a person is not shown an elephant passing through the eye of a needle. And from this he reasoned with his intellect that this is not literal swallowing, but rather the annihilation of the seven years of famine, which would consume and swallow and devour the seven years of plenty. Therefore Joseph began the interpretation with the seven bad ears of grain, to say that they would swallow and destroy the seven years of plenty, for it is impossible to interpret them otherwise. And they are the paradigm for all the details of the dream, since the things appear to be all one dream. And just as the seven empty and bad ears are seven years of famine, so the full ones are seven years of plenty, and so too is the matter of the cows." "And since the main proof that Joseph established for the entire interpretation was from the seven empty ears and from their swallowing of the good ones, therefore he said, after saying 'there shall be years of famine,' ״הוּא הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתִּי אֵת אֲשֶׁר הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׂה הֶרְאָה לְפַרְעֹה״ (Genesis 41:28) — for in this my opinion differed from the magicians: for they interpreted the dream concerning things that the Holy One, blessed be He, does through an emissary, such as the subduing of the concubines — the Holy One, blessed be He, does through an emissary; and so too the matter of childbirth is through an angel appointed over conception; and whatever is done through an emissary is not done as swiftly as things done by the Holy One, blessed be He, Himself. But the matter of sustenance, the Holy One, blessed be He, does Himself, not through an emissary, for four keys are in the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, and their mnemonic is 'key' (מַפְתֵּחַ): rain (מָטָר), sustenance (פַּרְנָסָה), revival (תְּחִיָּה), living creature (חַיָּה). Therefore Joseph said at the outset of his words, in response to what Pharaoh said, 'and no one declares it to me,' Joseph said, ״חֲלוֹם פַּרְעֹה אֶחָד הוּא״ (Genesis 41:25), and he needed to give a reason immediately for the doubling of the dream, and he said, ״אֵת אֲשֶׁר הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׂה הִגִּיד לְפַרְעֹה״ (Genesis 41:25) — for its interpretation concerns things that the Holy One, blessed be He, does Himself, not through an emissary; therefore the dream was repeated, for everything done by the Holy One, blessed be He, is done swiftly. And afterwards Joseph said this matter more explicitly, and said concerning the doubling of the dream, etc., ״כִּי נָכוֹן הַדָּבָר מֵעִם הָאֱלֹהִים וּמְמַהֵר הָאֱלֹהִים לַעֲשֹׂתוֹ״ (Genesis 41:32). And therefore Joseph said, ״הוּא הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתִּי אֲשֶׁר הָאֱלֹהִים עֹשֶׂה״ etc. (Genesis 41:28) — I have already prefaced for you that this dream concerns things that the Holy One, blessed be He, does Himself; but I had not yet proven that it would be as I say, that the entire interpretation concerns plenty and sustenance and food. But now that I see the matter of the swallowing of the empty ears of grain, which is impossible to interpret except as concerning the seven years of famine — if so, from here is proof for my words: 'it is the thing that I spoke — that which Elohim does,' that is, matters of sustenance, He has shown to Pharaoh, in order that he set right the matter of the famine, for it is in his power to act. And this interpretation is precious and clear." "<b>And what he said, 'And now let Pharaoh see.'</b> He used the expression 'and now' because Elohim hastens to do it; therefore he said 'and now,' that is, immediately and at once let Pharaoh see. And as for what the Ramban asked, 'was he given to the king as a counselor?' etc. — it seems to me that this is part of the interpretation, for after all he distanced the interpretation of the magicians because it was difficult for him to understand why YHWH showed precisely such a thing to Pharaoh, as explained above (Genesis 41:25). Therefore he said in his interpretation that this is why YHWH showed it specifically to Pharaoh — so that he would find a wise and discerning man to repair this breach."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:13.631145394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}